          "distinct": true,
          "id": "0571e1ab555432b7e9e2e13ad2ad0c7ce9a9cbc3",
          "message": "test(shacl): gate the FULL vendored W3C SHACL 1.2 suite in CI (sq-6glcr) [OPUS-4.8] (#1266)\n\nUntil now only tests/core/node/ (44) of the vendored SHACL 1.2 suite was\ngated; the rest of the 1.2 tree could regress unnoticed. This adds two\nmanifest-driven harnesses that walk the FULL trees with the same strict\nreport comparison (sh:conforms + bipartite 1:1 ValidationResult match,\nblank-node-tolerant) the existing harnesses use, each asserting a two-sided\nratchet (pass must not drop, gap must not grow) in BOTH feature states.\n\n- crates/sparq-shacl/tests/w3c_core_full_shacl12.rs: recurses\n  tests/core/manifest.ttl (complex/misc/node/path/property/targets/\n  validation-reports, 137 entries) — floor 114 default / 115 shacl-af,\n  fail-ceiling 22, per-category scoreboard.\n- crates/sparq-shacl/tests/w3c_sparql_shacl12.rs: walks\n  tests/sparql/manifest.ttl (24 entries) — floor 10, gap-ceiling 14, with\n  the 7 'mf:result sht:Failure' entries classed as ExpectedFailure (the\n  validator has no rejection channel yet) and asserted at exactly 7.\n- node-expr (65/65) already floored by w3c_node_expr{,_constraints}.\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: the W3C SHACL conformance job now also runs the\n  full-1.2 harnesses in both feature states; the existing 1.0/1.1\n  data-shapes gates are kept.\n- research/shacl12-conformance-gap.md: the honest per-category gap map, the\n  16 clusters, and the implementation beads sq-sx15d/rnkdh/mue75/0mjfd under\n  epic sq-waf9o, incl. the genuinely-draft zones (RDF-1.2 annotation parsing\n  + the 7 sht:Failure rejection tests).\n\nTEST + CI + DOC only — no crates/sparq-shacl/src/ change.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-27T16:22:32Z",
          "tree_id": "bf6d540733232df6b66d020f2832bb91d2013504",
