          "distinct": true,
          "id": "f3e8dcc8090909c032e433b0dc08e9930a7a5016",
          "message": "docs(research): design — shared zero-overhead eval substrate + reasoner suite + SERVICE federation + RSP/geo (sq-6tykl) [OPUS-4.8] (#1288)\n\nDesign-for-review records for the umbrella program sq-6tykl:\n\n- research/shared-eval-substrate.md (PRIMARY, sq-qonbz): extract the engine's\n  id-level join/numeric/term hot loops into a new leaf crate sparq-substrate\n  (depends only on sparq-core; monomorphic over Id=u32 + the SmallVec row/key\n  aliases; NO Box<dyn> on the hot path; feature-gated so the lean wasm bundle\n  stays byte-identical at floor 1686907). Corrects the brief: the reasoners do\n  NOT currently call the engine joins (they depend only on sparq-core and roll\n  their own FxHashMap adjacency), so this is an extract-and-unify project, not\n  reuse-as-is. Perf-neutrality proven by the deterministic byte ratchets + join\n  micro-benches on a pure-refactor-first PR.\n- research/reasoner-suite-on-substrate.md (sq-pbz04): RL-complete/EL/QL/Direct/\n  RIF/D sequenced by soundness risk; QL PerfectRef/tree-witness trap called out\n  (no Rust oracle exists; NP-complete UCQ minimisation); DL deferred (undecidable).\n- research/service-federation-conformance.md (sq-my8wd): wire sparql11/service\n  evaluation via real in-process sparq-server loopback endpoints (server APIs are\n  public; the Transport mock seam is only pub(crate)).\n- research/rsp-geo-conformance-integration.md (sq-2n1q3/sq-lk3aw): extend the\n  existing OGC geo ratchet; RSP/text framed honestly as expressivity/differential-\n  oracle ratchets (no W3C RSP conformance suite / no full-text RDF standard exist).\n\nDESIGN-FOR-REVIEW only; no engine/reasoner code changed. markdownlint-clean.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-29T11:42:08Z",
          "tree_id": "7ad992505f6dbbde3d768e420be109baf911a68a",
